      "overview": "Every picture-crafting mark you get in the WASSCE practical is earned on top of a sound workroom habit, so this first lesson is not housekeeping but syllabus. You will learn to name the supports used in a Ghanaian craft studio, from cartridge card through mount board to 3 mm masonite and plywood; to match adhesives to materials, including the traditional glair and the cassava starch paste made in the domestic kitchen; and to handle cutting tools, brushes, palettes and solvents without injury or wasted work. The lesson closes with the workroom rules and the tidiness marks, which examiners record under handling of materials in Paper 3. Nothing later in the course, from collage to framing, can be done safely or well unless this foundation is firm.",
