          "content": "A line is a point travelling in a path, and it does three jobs in a picture. It measures, since sighting a line with a pencil fixes the direction and length of an edge; it describes, because every outline of every object is a line; and it expresses, since the quality of the mark itself carries feeling. A straight vertical stands upright and quiet, a horizontal rests, a diagonal moves or falls, a curve breathes, and a broken jagged line irritates. Thickness and pressure matter as much as direction, so a 2B drawn with the side of the lead reads broad and soft while a 4H point reads thin and tense. Constructed line, made with ruler and compass for design work, must be even and unwavering; expressive line must be drawn from the shoulder in one sweep rather than scratched from the wrist, because a hairy outline can be corrected neither in force nor in accuracy.",
