        "id": "ex-pc-comp-1",
        "title": "Golden section construction on an A4 width",
        "problem": "A picture plane measures 210 mm by 297 mm. Locate the golden cut on the width, state the ratio being used, and check how far it falls from the nearest thirds line.",
        "stepByStepSolution": [
          "Step 1 (M1): State the condition of golden section: whole length : larger part = larger part : smaller part, a ratio of about 1 : 1.618.",
          "Step 2 (M1): Divide the width by the ratio to obtain the larger part: 210 / 1.618.",
          "Step 3 (A1): Evaluate: 210 / 1.618 is about 129.8 mm, so the golden cut falls at 130 mm from the left edge.",
          "Step 4 (M1): Find the smaller part by subtraction: 210 - 129.8 = 80.2 mm, and check the ratio 129.8 / 80.2, which is about 1.62.",
          "Step 5 (M1): Compare with the nearest thirds line: 2/3 of 210 = 140 mm, so the difference is 140 - 129.8 = 10.2 mm.",
          "Step 6 (A1): State the layout conclusion: the golden cut sits about 10 mm tighter than the right thirds line, so a focal mass placed there reads as settled rather than as mechanically divided."
        ],
        "keyTakeaway": "The golden section is a measurable division, and on A4 it lands about 10 mm inside the thirds line."
