        "id": "ex-pc-narrative-2",
        "title": "Building a thematic picture on \"Unity in Our School\"",
        "problem": "Set question: \"Illustrate the theme of unity in your school, using one symbolic object and a cool colour key.\" Decide the moment, the cast, the symbol and the palette, then justify each choice.",
        "stepByStepSolution": [
          "Step 1 (M1): Restate the theme as one sentence, \"different students finish one task together\", so every later choice can be tested against it.",
          "Step 2 (M1): Choose the moment after the effort, when the rope goes slack and everyone looks at the same place, because a completed shared act reads as unity more truly than a posed line.",
          "Step 3 (M1): Select a cast of five in odd grouping: two pulling, one steadying the rope, one carrying water, one watching from a lower step, with heads broken across three heights.",
          "Step 4 (A1): Fix the cool key: ultramarine and viridian grounds, Payne grey shadows, one ochre accent on the wooden handle of the rope so the symbol draws the eye.",
          "Step 5 (M1): Motivate the symbol inside the scene: a single plaited raffia cord, drawn clearly at the focal end of the rope, because plaited strands are literally many becoming one.",
          "Step 6 (A1): Compose on a shallow diagonal from the lower-left water cup to the upper-right raised hand, place the strongest value contrast at the plaited cord, and keep the school block pale in the background.",
          "Step 7 (A1): Appraise the finished sheet against the brief: theme stated without a caption, one motivated symbol, cool key held, setting recognisably a Ghanaian school compound."
        ],
        "keyTakeaway": "A theme is proved by a moment, a cast and one motivated object, not by a written word on the picture."
